cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying experiments, please cite the paper listed under preferred-citation."
title: "rf-plateau-hpo: Adaptive Random Forest n_estimators Tuning with Triplet-Based Plateau Search and Optuna"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of triplet-based PLATEAU search for selecting a
  near-minimal sufficient number of trees (n_estimators, ensemble size) in a
  Random Forest, integrated with Optuna/TPE hyperparameter optimization.
  Instead of sampling n_estimators from a predefined range, the ensemble size
  is adapted across HPO trials from relative changes of the out-of-bag score
  at a geometric triplet of forest sizes, under a user-specified relative
  tolerance. Includes Hyperband/BOHB-style and fixed-range TPE baselines, a
  declarative dataset registry, and full reproducibility material for the
  IEEE Access 2026 paper.
